--TEST--
Core\Imap::open throws `RuntimeError` for a granted name with no `[imap.<name>]` block, and for a block with no sign-in, before any connection is opened — `rule:core-classes/imap`
--FILE--
<?nvs
// `imap.connect` grants `inbox`, but `nvs.toml` has no `[imap.inbox]` block.
try {
    var $inbox = Core\Imap::open("inbox");
    echo "opened inbox", "\n";
} catch (RuntimeError $missing) {
    echo $missing->message, "\n";
}

// `[imap.shared]` has a server and no `user` or `password`.
// A mailbox always needs a sign-in, so `open` throws.
try {
    var $shared = Core\Imap::open("shared");
    echo "opened shared", "\n";
} catch (RuntimeError $missing) {
    echo $missing->message, "\n";
}
--FILE nvs.toml--
[capabilities.imap]
connect = ["inbox", "shared"]

[imap.shared]
host = "127.0.0.1"
port = 1
--EXPECT--
Core\Imap::open: no `[imap.inbox]` block sets `host`, so there is no mailbox of that name to open
Core\Imap::open: `[imap.shared]` sets no `user` and `password`, and a mailbox always needs a sign-in
